    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byblos">Byblos</a>, on the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a>, is one of the oldest continuously inhabited towns in the world.</li><li>For over two thousand years it shipped cedar and resin to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, absorbing Egyptian culture and religion.</li><li>Its royal inscriptions are among the earliest in the Phoenician alphabet, ancestor of the Greek and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> scripts.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papyrus">papyrus</a> byblos after the city through which they obtained it, and from that word came biblion, book, and ultimately the word Bible.</p></aside>
    </section>

